<title>HONG KONG: New World Infra interim net rises 28 pct.</title>
<headline>New World Infra interim net rises 28 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   36.4   vs  33.6</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    nil    vs  nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  nil    vs  nil</p>
<p>    Net			    273.42 vs  213.47</p>
<p>    Turnover		     313.83 vs  186.59</p>
<p>    Company name		 New World Infrastructure Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  N/A</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - New World Infrastructure is a subsidiary of New World Development Co Ltd.</p>
<p>The company's financial year end date has been changed to June 30 from December 31 to make it coterminous with that of New World Development.</p>
